{{Documentation/Header}}
Shared documentation for '''[[Module:JST]] and the JST date templates'''.

The wiki server runs on '''UTC''', but this wiki's subject matter is Japan-centric, so dates shown to readers should be '''Japan Standard Time''' (JST, UTC+9). This module returns the current JST date and time in a chosen format, and each template below is a one-line wrapper around one format code.

Internally the module takes the current UTC timestamp and adds 32,400 seconds — exactly nine hours — then formats the result. JST has no daylight saving and no sub-hour offset, so the shift is constant year-round.

== The templates ==
None of these take parameters. Each one simply calls the module with its format code.

