An unrecognised format code returns an '''empty string''', not an error.

== Which to use ==
MediaWiki's own <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTYEAR}}</nowiki></code>, <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTHOUR}}</nowiki></code> and friends report '''server time (UTC)'''. Use the JST templates above wherever a date is shown to readers or compared against Japanese dates.

There is no built-in <code>CURRENTMINUTE</code> or <code>CURRENTSECOND</code> magic word in MediaWiki, which is why {{T|CURRENTMINUTE}} and {{T|CURRENTSECOND}} carry no <code>JST</code> in their names — they are not shadowing anything. Minutes and seconds are identical in both zones regardless, since JST is a whole-hour offset.

{{Notice
| header = {{T|CURRENTDATE}} is not part of this family
| info = {{T|CURRENTDATE}} is built from the '''UTC''' magic words <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTYEAR}}-{{CURRENTMONTH}}-{{CURRENTDAY2}}</nowiki></code>, despite its similar name. Mixing it with the JST templates on one page can show two different dates for the nine hours each day when the two zones disagree.
| border = orange
}}

== Zero-padding ==
<code>m</code>, <code>d</code>, <code>H</code>, <code>i</code> and <code>s</code> are always padded to two digits; <code>Y</code> is not. The padding matters: {{T|ProcessBirthdayCategory}} and {{T|Birthday Calendar}} match against categories like <code><nowiki>[[Category:Birthday/06/30]]</nowiki></code>, so <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTJSTMONTH}}</nowiki></code> can be passed straight through, while a hand-typed <code>6</code> would match nothing.

